# CVEs with fix versions identified by Trivy but not yet available in the
# AL2023 package repositories. Remove entries once the fixed packages land.
#
# All entries verified 2026-10-28 via `dnf list --showduplicates <pkg>`
# against the live AL2023 repo mirror inside
# 1121citrus/aws-backup-base:1.2.2 -- no build matching the "Fixed Version"
# Trivy reports exists yet for any entry below. The curl-minimal,
# cyrus-sasl-lib, libcap, libcurl-minimal, pcre2/pcre2-syntax, and
# python3/python3-libs entries are inherited from aws-backup-base and
# mirror its own .trivyignore (same repo-mirror propagation gap, verified
# independently here). The python3.12/python3.12-libs entries are specific
# to this image, which installs python3.12 itself (not part of the base
# image). The prior single entry (CVE-2026-14456,
# openssl-fips-provider-latest/openssl-libs) is resolved as of
# aws-backup-base 1.2.2's 2026-10-28 AL2023 digest refresh and has been
# removed.
#
# ca-certificates re-verified 2026-10-29 via the same method: neither
# .0.4 nor .0.5 exists on the mirror yet. These two entries were already
# tracked in .grype.yaml/SECURITY.md (ALAS2023-2026-3306) but had been
# omitted from this file, which is why Trivy gated while Grype did not.

# curl-minimal / libcurl-minimal: HTTP/2 upload Use-After-Free — fix:
# 8.21.0-5.amzn2023.0.3 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-92392

# cyrus-sasl-lib: heap buffer overflow in add_to_challenge() allows
# malicious server to crash client — fix: 2.1.27-18.amzn2023.0.4 (not yet
# in repo)
CVE-2026-107161

# libcap: upstream Go net/http advisories misattributed by Trivy's AL2023
# feed to this package's NVR — fix: 2.73-1.amzn2023.0.8 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-78659
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-94440

# pcre2 / pcre2-syntax: out-of-bounds write/read via crafted regular
# expressions and invalid UTF matching — fix: 10.40-1.amzn2023.0.5 (not
# yet in repo)
CVE-2026-103111
CVE-2026-86145
CVE-2026-89156
CVE-2026-89160

# python3 / python3-libs: certificate verification bypass via missing
# server_hostname validation in SSLContext.wrap_bio() — fix:
# 3.9.25-1.amzn2023.0.11 (not yet in repo). Shared with python3.12 below.
CVE-2026-19553

# python3.12 / python3.12-libs (installed directly by this image's own
# Dockerfile, not inherited from aws-backup-base): multiple CVEs — fix:
# 3.12.15-2.amzn2023.0.1 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-15310
CVE-2026-15806
CVE-2026-17084
CVE-2026-19445
CVE-2026-19672
CVE-2026-82049
CVE-2026-87910

# ca-certificates: Firefox website spoofing via failure to block
# compromised intermediate certificates (fix: 2025.2.76-1.0.amzn2023.0.4)
# and eMudhra intermediate CA distrust (fix:
# 2025.2.76-1.0.amzn2023.0.5) — neither build is on the mirror yet
CVE-2026-113470
CVE-2026-114406
